title: The Death of Pavel Axelrod
view-if: year = 1928 and month >= 4
frequency: 1000
max-visits: 1
tags: event
go-to: pm if chancellor = "Axelrod"; not_pm if chancellor != "Axelrod"
on-arrival: axelrod_dead = 1; n_advisors -= 1 if axelrod_advisor == 1; axelrod_advisor = 0;
new-page: true
face-image: img/portraits/Axelrod.jpg

= The Death of Pavel Axelrod

@pm
on-arrival: axelrod_died_in_office = 1
# TODO: achievement for axelrod dying in office

Government Chairman Pavel Axelrod has died while in office. He will be greatly missed. But now, we must select a new Government Chairman.

- @lozovsky_chancellor: Solomon Lozovsky (RSDRP) for Government Chairman.
- @martov_chancellor: Yuliy Martov (RSDRP) for Government Chairman.
- @dan_chancellor: Fyodor Dan (RSDRP) for Government Chairman.
- @kerensky_chancellor: Let Alexander Kerensky of the PSR become Government Chairman.
- @avksentyev_chancellor: Nikolay Avksentyev of the PSR should be Government Chairman.
- @zenzinov_chancellor: Vladimir Zenzinov of the PSR should be Government Chairman.
- @odinets: Dmitry Odinets has threatened to sink the coalition if we fail to concede the Chairmanship.

@lozovsky_chancellor
on-arrival: chancellor = "Lozovsky"; chancellor_party = "RSDRP"; psr_relation -= 5; kadets_relation -= 5; rkp_relation += 5
view-if: psr_party_leader != "Odinets"
subtitle: The Socialist-Revolutionaries are worried about giving power to a former Bolshevik.

Our coalition partners are reluctant to accept the new Government Chairman, but they do not make loud objections.

@martov_chancellor
on-arrival: chancellor = "Martov"; chancellor_party = "RSDRP"; psr_relation -= 3; kadets_relation -= 3
view-if: psr_party_leader != "Odinets"
subtitle: He is a good organizer and party leader, but is he also a good chairman?

Our coalition partners are reluctant to accept the new Government Chairman, but they do not make loud objections.

@dan_chancellor
on-arrival: chancellor = "Dan"; chancellor_party = "RSDRP"; psr_relation -= 3; kadets_relation -= 3; rkp_relation -= 5
view-if: psr_party_leader != "Odinets"
subtitle: The Socialist-Revolutionary Party is worried about his calls for expanding our electoral base into the countryside.

Our coalition partners are reluctant to accept the new Government Chairman, but they do not make loud objections.

@kerensky_chancellor
on-arrival: chancellor = "Kerensky"; chancellor_party = "PSR"; psr_relation += 5; kadets_relation += 5
view-if: psr_party_leader != "Odinets"
subtitle: The Socialist-Revolutionary Party claims it is their turn...

The Socialist-Revolutionaries and sympathetic Liberals are grateful that we have supported Alexander Kerensky for Government Chairman.

@avksentyev_chancellor
on-arrival: chancellor = "Avksentyev"; chancellor_party = "PSR"; psr_relation += 5; kadets_relation += 2
view-if: psr_party_leader != "Odinets"
subtitle: As a moderate member of the Socialist-Revolutionary Party, he could represent unity.

Our coalition partners accept Nikolay Avksentyev of the Socialist-Revolutionary Party as the new Government Chairman.

@zenzinov_chancellor
on-arrival: chancellor = "Zenzinov"; chancellor_party = "PSR"; psr_relation += 5
view-if: psr_party_leader = "Zenzinov"
subtitle: As a sympathetic member of the Socialist-Revolutionary Party, he could represent unity.

Our coalition partners accept Vladimir Zenzinov of the Socialist-Revolutionary Party as the new Government Chairman.

@odinets
on-arrival: chancellor = "Odinets"; chancellor_party = "PSR"; psr_relation += 5; psr_party_leader = "Odinets"
view-if: psr_party_leader = "Odinets"
subtitle: Odinets, supported by the Nationalist and Conservative Esers, has demanded we support his appointment as Government Chairman.

Our party is all but unanimously against this, and if we follow through with his demands it will cause a storm internally. Many within the party are calling for an end to our coalition, and that we cease working with the PSR until Odinets is removed.

- @new_elections: We will host a Vote of No-Confidence and bring down the governing Coalition, ushering in new elections.
- @youcantconcedetodmitryodinetsyoufuckingidiot: Let Dmitry Odinets of the PSR become Government Chairman.

@new_elections
subtitle:
on-arrival: rsdrp_in_government = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; chancellor = "Zarudny"; chancellor_party = "PSR"; next_election_time = time + 3 if next_election_time > time+3; next_election_month = month + 3 if next_election_time >= time+3; next_election_year = year if next_election_time >= time+3; next_election_year += 1 if next_election_month > 12; next_election_month -= 12 if next_election_month > 12; rsdrp_toleration = 0; left_strength += 8; pro_republic -= 5; new_middle_rsdrp -= 3; rural_rsdrp -= 3; old_middle_rsdrp -= 3; catholics_rsdrp -= 3

We have called for a vote of no confidence ourselves, and have brought down this government. Chancellor [+ chancellor +], a respected Narodist Lawyer, currently rules as acting chancellor until a new government can be formed.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@youcantconcedetodmitryodinetsyoufuckingidiot
subtitle: You shouldn't see this, so this will do the exact same thing as calling new elections. Fuck you.
